.TH GITEA-SYNC-ALL.SH 1 "2026-04-25" "GitMirror" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
gitea-sync-all.sh \- trigger mirror sync for all mirror repositories in a Gitea user account
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bash gitea-sync-all.sh
.RI [ config.json ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B gitea-sync-all.sh
enumerates repositories for the configured Gitea user, filters to mirror repositories, and calls the Gitea
.B /mirror-sync
API endpoint for each mirror.
.PP
The script prints per-repository results and a final run summary including attempted, synced, and failed counts.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.I config.json
Optional path to configuration file. Defaults to
.B config.json
in the current working directory.
.SH CONFIGURATION
The script reads these keys from the config file:
.TP
.B GITEA_URL
Base URL of the Gitea instance.
.TP
.B GITEA_USER
Gitea username whose repositories are scanned.
.TP
.B GITEA_TOKEN
Gitea API token with permission to trigger mirror sync.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Returns 0 on completion. Returns 2 for missing prerequisites or invalid configuration. Returns 3 if repository listing fails.
.SH EXAMPLES
Sync all mirrors using default config file:
.PP
.B bash gitea-sync-all.sh
.PP
Sync all mirrors with an explicit config file:
.PP
.B bash gitea-sync-all.sh ./config.json
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR git-mirror.sh (1),
.BR gitea-prune-orphans.sh (1)
